Package: bibliograph-web
Version: @VERSION@
Section: web
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Maintainer: Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>
Homepage: https://biblio.livtet.olamaelcu.net
Depends: nodejs (>= 20), adduser, bibliograph-happyview
Recommends: nginx
Description: Bibliograph web edge (SvelteKit appview front end)
 The public SvelteKit application for Bibliograph. It serves the UI and the
 /xrpc surface, and is the only public origin: queries and procedures are
 proxied server-side to HappyView on 127.0.0.1:3000, with the edge's own XRPC
 client identity injected so a browser cannot choose it.
 .
 The adapter-node build is self-contained JavaScript (~2 MB) and runs on the
 host's nodejs; no runtime is bundled. Configuration lives in
 /etc/bibliograph/web.env — the HappyView client key and secret are required
 for the proxy to identify itself upstream.
 .
 The service binds 127.0.0.1:5176. Put a TLS-terminating reverse proxy in front
 (the package recommends nginx); the port and HappyView URL are conffile
 settings.
